---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "@/config/site";

const lastUpdated = "2 September 2026";

const sections = [
  { id: "what-are-cookies", label: "1. What are cookies" },
  { id: "how-we-use-cookies", label: "2. How we use cookies" },
  { id: "types", label: "3. Types of cookies on this site" },
  { id: "third-party", label: "4. Third-party cookies" },
  { id: "duration", label: "5. How long cookies last" },
  { id: "managing", label: "6. Managing and disabling cookies" },
  { id: "do-not-track", label: "7. Do Not Track signals" },
  { id: "changes", label: "8. Changes to this policy" },
  { id: "contact", label: "9. Contact us" },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="How JM Travels uses cookies and similar technologies on this website.">
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-jm max-w-3xl prose-copy space-y-6 text-body text-charcoal">
      <h1 class="text-display-l text-navy">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-body-s text-slate">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This Cookie Policy explains how {site.legalName} ("JM Travels", "we", "us" or "our") uses cookies and
        similar technologies on this website, what they do, and the choices available to you. It should be read
        alongside our <a href="/privacy-policy" class="link-editorial">Privacy Policy</a>, which explains more
        broadly how we handle personal information.
      </p>

      <nav aria-label="Table of contents" class="card-surface shadow-soft p-6">
        <p class="text-label text-slate mb-3">On this page</p>
        <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-1 list-none pl-0 text-body-s">
          {sections.map((s) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`} class="link-editorial">{s.label}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <h2 id="what-are-cookies" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">1. What are cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. They are widely used to make
        websites function properly, to remember your preferences, and to help site owners understand how their
        website is used. "Similar technologies" includes things like local storage, which some browser features and
        scripts use in a comparable way.
      </p>

      <h2 id="how-we-use-cookies" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">2. How we use cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use a deliberately minimal set of cookies: those required for the website to function correctly, and,
        where enabled, an analytics cookie that helps us understand overall traffic patterns so we can improve the
        site. We do not use cookies to build advertising profiles, and we do not sell or share cookie data with
        advertisers.
      </p>

      <h2 id="types" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">3. Types of cookies on this site</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>
          <strong>Strictly necessary cookies:</strong> required for core site functionality, such as remembering
          that you have interacted with certain interface elements during your visit. The site cannot function
          properly without these, and they do not require consent under most data protection laws.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics / performance cookies:</strong> where enabled, we use an analytics tool (currently
          Google Analytics, if configured) to understand which pages are visited, how visitors arrived at the site,
          and general, aggregated usage patterns. This information is used in an aggregated form and is not used to
          personally identify you for marketing purposes.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use advertising cookies, cross-site tracking cookies, or social media tracking pixels.</p>

      <h2 id="third-party" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">4. Third-party cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Where analytics is enabled, cookies may be set by our analytics provider (Google Analytics) in accordance
        with its own privacy and cookie practices. We do not control these third-party cookies directly; you can
        find more information in{" "}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link-editorial">
          Google's own cookie policy
        </a>. If, in the future, we embed third-party content on this site (for example, a map), that provider may
        also set its own cookies when that content loads.
      </p>

      <h2 id="duration" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">5. How long cookies last</h2>
      <p>
        Some cookies are "session" cookies, which are deleted automatically when you close your browser. Others are
        "persistent" cookies, which remain on your device for a set period (or until you delete them) so the site
        can recognise you on a return visit. Analytics cookies, where enabled, are typically persistent and are
        governed by the retention periods set by the analytics provider.
      </p>

      <h2 id="managing" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">6. Managing and disabling cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Most browsers allow you to view, manage, delete and block cookies through their settings. Because the exact
        steps vary by browser, we recommend checking your browser's help documentation (for example, searching
        "manage cookies" for Chrome, Safari, Firefox or Edge). Disabling non-essential cookies will not prevent you
        from using the core parts of this website, though some features that rely on remembering your preferences
        may not work as intended.
      </p>

      <h2 id="do-not-track" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">7. Do Not Track signals</h2>
      <p>
        Some browsers offer a "Do Not Track" (DNT) signal. There is currently no unified industry standard for how
        websites should respond to DNT signals, so this site does not currently respond differently when a DNT
        signal is detected. You can still manage cookies directly through your browser settings as described above.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the cookies and technologies we
        use, or for legal reasons. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page indicates when it was last
        revised.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact" class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">9. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`} class="link-editorial">{site.contact.email}</a>, or via the{" "}
        <a href="/contact" class="link-editorial">Contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="text-body-s text-slate pt-6 border-t border-mist">
        This policy is provided as a general, good-faith description of our cookie practices and does not
        constitute legal advice. It should be reviewed by a qualified legal professional familiar with the specific
        jurisdictions in which JM Travels operates before being relied upon as a complete compliance measure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
